# Dual theme requirement

The site has two live themes until the owner explicitly removes one:

- **Calicon** — steel-grey + gold marketing chrome (`data-theme="calicon"`)
- **Canvas Group** — dark editorial shell with hamburger rail (`data-theme="canvas"`)

Default theme is Canvas. Users can switch. Do not treat either as disposable.

## Do this on every UI, content, routing, or layout change

- Implement the change so **both** themes show the correct result — not only the theme currently on screen.
- Prefer **one shared page/content source** styled through existing tokens and theme CSS. Do not fork duplicate pages per theme unless the shells truly cannot share markup.
- If chrome differs (header, nav, home, footer), update **both shells**: Calicon `SiteHeader` / `SiteFooter` and Canvas `src/components/canvas/*`.
- After the change, **verify both themes** (switch the selector, check the same routes and states). A single-theme check is incomplete.
- Watch for regressions: hardcoded `slate-*` / gold-only styles, Calicon-only headers, Canvas homepage replacing inner pages, missing nav links, unredacted assets.

This rule stands until the user says a theme is removed.
